  "description": "Acme API Hub, launched on\u202fJanuary\u202f15\u202f2023 and most recently updated on\u202fNovember\u202f20\u202f2024, is a curated collection of web services offered by Acme\u202fCorp.\u202fThe hub\u2019s landing page can be reached at\u202fhttps://api.acme.com/apis.json, and the corporate logo \u2013\u202fhttps://acme.com/logo.png\u202f\u2013 provides a visual identifier for the catalogue.\u202fThis service conforms to version\u202f0.14 of the APIs\u2011json specification and is described as \u201cA collection of APIs provided by Acme Corp.\u201d\u202fThe hub is tagged with the keywords **finance** and **api\u2011hub** to aid discovery.\n\nAmong the offerings, the Acme Payments API (https://api.acme.com/payments) delivers payment\u2011processing capabilities.\u202fIts documentation and contract are available via a Swagger definition at\u202fhttps://api.acme.com/payments/swagger.json, while pricing details are published at\u202fhttps://acme.com/payments/pricing.\u202fThe API is illustrated by the image\u202fhttps://api.acme.com/payments/logo.png, carries the tags **payments** and **v1**, and is marked as \u201cstable\u201d in its metadata.\u202fFor support, John\u202fDoe (john.doe@acme.com) of Acme\u202fCorp can be contacted at\u202f+1\u2011555\u20111234 or through the support portal\u202fhttps://acme.com/support; his Twitter handle is\u202f@acme_support.\u202fThe overall hub is maintained by Jane\u202fSmith (jane.smith@acme.com), also of Acme\u202fCorp, reachable at\u202f+1\u2011555\u20115678 and listed on GitHub under\u202facme/maintainer.\u202fAdditionally, the hub references the Acme Shipping API, whose definition can be found at\u202fhttps://api.acme.com/shipping/apis.json."
}